      "writtenOn": "2021-11-29T15:28:31Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Before we get too far into the BackendTexture implementation, I just want to make sure we\u0027re all happy with their API and what we want to support in regards to them. I\u0027ve add a few comments/question to start the discussion, but would love to hear others opinions.",
      "revId": "0d1d440444d8b479b94b799f56c7efe44c9e00bf",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "1b656072_5e1afeaa",
        "filename": "experimental/graphite/include/BackendTexture.h",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 25,
      "author": {
        "id": 5036
      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-11-29T15:28:31Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Should BackendTexture we taking a ref to the Mtl Textures? For Vulkan and D3D (and Ganesh GL) the BackendTexture does not hold a ref of the backend object. Instead these are all treated as raw handles and the client is required to keep the backend object alive as long as the BackendTexture is wrapped in a Skia object. So we could match that same system in Metal by only taking a mtl::Handle instead (i.e. id\u003cMTLTexture\u003e). This would allow the client to think of all backends the same.\n\nIf we do this, the question becomes what do we do internally in mtl::Texture. Right now that class holds an sk_cfp\u003cid\u003cMTLTexture\u003e\u003e. It is a little weird for us to internally take a ref to the texture when publicly we\u0027re telling the client they have to keep the object alive. Maybe its not weird for metal to be taking a ref to the object since the metal api itself is a ref counted API so we should stick to that model.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 25,
        "startChar": 39,
        "endLine": 25,
        "endChar": 46
      },
      "revId": "0d1d440444d8b479b94b799f56c7efe44c9e00bf",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "f466ac28_c17ea7f1",
        "filename": "experimental/graphite/include/BackendTexture.h",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 25,
      "author": {
        "id": 5065
      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-11-29T16:26:42Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I don\u0027t see that we have much choice but to use sk_cfp\u003c\u003e in mtl::Texture. If we\u0027re creating our own textures, we need to keep them alive and we don\u0027t want to manage lifetime manually (and I\u0027m not sure we\u0027d want to distinguish between wrapped and non-wrapped textures to know whether to de-ref on destruction). And in D3D we do keep a ref to the backend object, as ID3D12Resource is ref-counted as well.",
      "parentUuid": "1b656072_5e1afeaa",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 25,
        "startChar": 39,
        "endLine": 25,
        "endChar": 46
      },
      "revId": "0d1d440444d8b479b94b799f56c7efe44c9e00bf",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "a3363ca4_a1142984",
        "filename": "experimental/graphite/include/BackendTexture.h",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 25,
      "author": {
        "id": 5036
      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-11-29T18:29:57Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Yeah I think we want an sk_cfp in mtl::Texture for all use cases. I am leaning towards not reffing the mtl::Handle in backend texture.\n\nWe would just have to be very explicit in the API for wrapping on what the clients responsibility for the lifetime of the backend object is. On metal the client is safe to drop their refs on the object as soon as it is wrapped in Skia. For Vulkan they are required to keep the object alive until Skia is done with it. For D3D, I guess it would be similar to Metal. We could just say for all backends the client should keep the object alive until Skia is done just to be safe. But obviously this is a slight waste for clients only using metal.",
      "parentUuid": "f466ac28_c17ea7f1",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 25,
        "startChar": 39,
        "endLine": 25,
        "endChar": 46
      },
      "revId": "0d1d440444d8b479b94b799f56c7efe44c9e00bf",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "98ccd95a_0f34c3f1",
        "filename": "experimental/graphite/include/BackendTexture.h",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
