      "lineNbr": 93,
      "author": {
        "id": 5036
      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-11-29T15:33:00Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Oh another question, Should calling context-\u003edestroyBackendTexture(backendTexture), clear out the backendTexture (i.e. set it to be invalid) or just leave everything as is? Currently Ganesh just leaves it as is since the dtor on most backends doesn\u0027t do anything anyways. But with Metal this means the MTLTexture doesn\u0027t get destroyed until the ~BackendTexture. We could unref the texture here instead.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 91,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 93,
        "endChar": 1
      },
      "revId": "0d1d440444d8b479b94b799f56c7efe44c9e00bf",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "562c19c0_893b6ebb",
        "filename": "experimental/graphite/src/mtl/MtlGpu.mm",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 93,
      "author": {
        "id": 5065
      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-11-29T16:26:42Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "If we store mtl::Handle then we don\u0027t need to do anything, right? The client is responsible for unref-ing the ref keeping the BackendTexture alive.",
      "parentUuid": "eb606fa5_0595afca",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 91,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 93,
        "endChar": 1
      },
      "revId": "0d1d440444d8b479b94b799f56c7efe44c9e00bf",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "9954b974_f48ba066",
        "filename": "experimental/graphite/src/mtl/MtlGpu.mm",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 93,
      "author": {
        "id": 5036
      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-11-29T18:29:57Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Well if we only had a mtl::Handle (without reffing it by the BackendTexture) then we would have to do an unref here since it has to pair with the ref on create. The API already requires the if you use Context::createBackendTexture then you must call Context::deleteBackendTexture. So those would be paired up.",
      "parentUuid": "562c19c0_893b6ebb",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 91,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 93,
        "endChar": 1
      },
      "revId": "0d1d440444d8b479b94b799f56c7efe44c9e00bf",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "4d783a8e_0d471dad",
        "filename": "experimental/graphite/src/mtl/MtlGpu.mm",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 93,
      "author": {
        "id": 5065
      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-11-29T21:42:51Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Oh right. So just to confirm -- we need the extra ref on a client\u0027s BackendTexture because like Texture we need to maintain lifetime when we create one ourselves.",
      "parentUuid": "9954b974_f48ba066",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 91,
